From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:58:48 +0000
Subject: media: videobuf2: dma-contig: fix cache maintenance of non-coherent
 buffers

The dma-buf begin_cpu_access() and end_cpu_access() callbacks were
reduced to stubs when V4L2_FLAG_MEMORY_NON_CONSISTENT was removed, as
every dma-contig buffer was coherent at the time. Non-coherent MMAP
buffers were then reintroduced with V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT, but
the callbacks were not restored, so DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC on an exported
non-coherent buffer does no cache maintenance.

A CAPTURE buffer that is queued with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_NO_CACHE_CLEAN and
V4L2_BUF_FLAG_NO_CACHE_INVALIDATE and is then read through its dma-buf
gets stale cache lines. With FFmpeg mapping Amlogic decoder frames this
way the frame checksums are wrong.

Sync the buffer for the CPU in begin_cpu_access() and for the device in
end_cpu_access(), matching what vb2_dc_finish() and vb2_dc_prepare() do.

The pages from dma_alloc_noncontiguous() are also zeroed through the
cache, and must be synced for the device before it first writes them.
vb2 relies on the sync in vb2_dc_prepare() for that, which the cache
hints skip, so dirty lines of the zeroed buffer can be written back over
the first frame decoded into it, as 64-byte runs of zeros. Sync a new
non-coherent buffer for the device when it is allocated.

Fixes: de27891f675e ("media: videobuf2: handle non-contiguous DMA allocations")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c | 21 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c
+++ b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-dma-contig.c
@@ -220,6 +220,7 @@ static int vb2_dc_alloc_non_coherent(struct vb2_dc_buf *buf)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	buf->dma_addr = sg_dma_address(buf->dma_sgt->sgl);
+	dma_sync_sgtable_for_device(buf->dev, buf->dma_sgt, buf->dma_dir);
 
 	/*
 	 * For non-coherent buffers the kernel mapping is created on demand
@@ -428,6 +429,16 @@ static int
 vb2_dc_dmabuf_ops_begin_cpu_access(struct dma_buf *dbuf,
 				   enum dma_data_direction direction)
 {
+	struct vb2_dc_buf *buf = dbuf->priv;
+
+	if (!buf->non_coherent_mem)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (buf->vaddr)
+		invalidate_kernel_vmap_range(buf->vaddr, buf->size);
+
+	dma_sync_sgtable_for_cpu(buf->dev, buf->dma_sgt, buf->dma_dir);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -435,6 +446,16 @@ static int
 vb2_dc_dmabuf_ops_end_cpu_access(struct dma_buf *dbuf,
 				 enum dma_data_direction direction)
 {
+	struct vb2_dc_buf *buf = dbuf->priv;
+
+	if (!buf->non_coherent_mem)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (buf->vaddr)
+		flush_kernel_vmap_range(buf->vaddr, buf->size);
+
+	dma_sync_sgtable_for_device(buf->dev, buf->dma_sgt, buf->dma_dir);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
